(Plaintiff purchased a 2014 Volvo VNL diesel semi-truck from Diamond for $27,092.75. Diamond knowingly concealed a material DEF/SCR emissions defect rendering the truck non-compliant with CA emissions law and unfit for lawful highway operation. The truck entered limp mode shortly after purchase. Plaintiff seeks rescission, $25,968.65 in out-of-pocket losses \($20,218.65 documented, $5,750 by sworn testimony\), $23,400 lost commercial income \(conservative\), $4,302.55 prejudgment interest, $25,000 punitive damages, declaratory relief, and costs. Total judgment requested: not less than $78,671.20 plus costs. Alpine is sued as Diamond's successor/alter ego. See Attachment 4b.) Tj
ET
Q
EMC
Q

endstream
